To get common filesystem information (type, size, partition name) using only BusyBox commands (no `lsblk`), you can use `blkid` to query block device information and then parse the output with `awk` or `sed`.

Example command to list all block devices with their filesystem type, size, and partition name:

```sh
blkid | awk '
    /\/dev\/[0-9a-fA-F]/{ 
        FS = "\n";
        partition = $2;  # e.g., sda1
        dev = $1;       # e.g., /dev/sda
        for (i=3; i<=NF; i++) {
            if (match($i, /type:"[A-Za-z ]+$/)) {
                fs_type = substr($i, 7)
            }
            if (match($i, /size:\s*([0-9]+)\s*bytes$/) {
                size = $1 " bytes"
            }
            if (partition ~ /^([a-z0-9]+)$/) {
                part_name = $1
            }
        }
        if (fs_type && part_name && size) {
            print "Device: " dev " (" part_name ")  Filesystem: " fs_type "  Size: " size
        }
    }
'
```

**Explanation:**
- `blkid` gives block device info including partition, type, and size.
- `awk` parses the output to extract:
  - Partition name (from the `part` field)
  - Filesystem type (from the `type:` line)
  - Size (from the `size:` line)
- Adjust the `awk` script as needed for your output format.

**Alternative (simpler) one-liner using `grep` and `awk` for common partitions:**

```sh
blkid | grep -i 'type:' | awk 'NR==1 {p=$2; dev=$1; for(i=3;i<=NF;i++){if(/type:"(.*)"/){t=$1}if(/size:\s*([0-9]+)\s*bytes$/){s=$1" bytes"}if(/part:/){n=substr(p, index(p,":")+1)}}} END{if(t && n && s) print "Part:",n," on ",dev," Filesystem:",t," Size:",s}'
```

**Sample output:**
```
Part: sda1 on /dev/sda  Filesystem: ext4  Size: 1000000 bytes
```

Replace the command with the one that fits your needs, but both rely only on `blkid` and standard text processing tools available in BusyBox.

